@page "/miscellaneous"

<Page PageName="Miscellaneous" ShowTitle="false">
    <Example Header="Splash Screen" CodeFile="Splash.txt">
        <Text>
            There is no splash screen component, but css that can be used to create splash screen.
            Replace the code from this example with the <code>@("<div id=\"app\">")</code> in <i>`index.html`</i>.
            The <code>--splash-height</code> and <code>--splash-width</code> css variables can be used to adjust 
            the height and width of logo and progress bar.
        </Text>
        <div class="splash-wrapper">
            <div class="splash">
                <img src="./images/shine.svg" alt="Shine Blazor" class="logo text-primary" />
                <div class="progress">
                    <div class="progress-bar"></div>
                </div>
                <div class="progress-text"></div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </Example>

    <Example Header="Theme Selector" CodeFile="ThemeSelector.txt">
        <Text>
            Shine Blazor provides a built-in component to switch between dark and light theme. 
            To create custom theme override <code>ShineBlazor.Components.Theme.DefaultTheme</code>.
            The <code>ShineBlazor.Components.Theme.ThemeSelector</code> component can be placed 
            anywhere inside the layout.
        </Text>
        <Text>
            You can also have a custom icon, button or switch to change the theme and hide the button from 
            this component by setting <code>ShowThemeSwitch="false"</code> and using <code>DarkMode</code> 
            parameter.
        </Text>
    </Example>
</Page>